# Component structure

- Prefer small, focused components. When a file grows large (hundreds of lines), extract subcomponents, hooks, or helpers into colocated files in the same folder.
- Keep the default export readable: orchestration at the top level, details in named subcomponents or `use*` hooks.
- Reuse shared UI from workspace packages (e.g. `@wisihe/ui-react`) before duplicating markup.
- **`@wisihe/ui-react`** — atoms and molecules (Button, Card, Pagination, Breadcrumbs, SectionHeader, etc.). Use Tailwind `flex`/`grid` for layout in apps. Documented in Storybook (`apps/ui-docs`).
- **`app/components/effects/`** — site-specific motion/visual FX (Dock, ScrollStack, CircularGallery). Lazy-load with `next/dynamic` at call sites.
- **`app/components/{domain}/`** — CMS-backed sections and page composition (marketing, paintings, projects, …).

## Storybook (`apps/ui-docs`)

Stories live in `@wisihe/ui-react` (colocated `*.stories.tsx`) and `apps/ui-docs/src/stories/` (tokens, app-only docs).

**Sidebar structure** (top-level order is fixed in `preview.ts`):

1. **Design System** — `Atoms/*` and `Molecules/*` (Button, Dialog, RecipeMetaBadges, …)
2. **Cards** — domain views: `Painting/*`, `Project/*`, `Photography/*`
3. **Effects** — motion/visual FX (e.g. BrushReveal)
4. **Tokens** — design token reference (e.g. Color)

**Adding or renaming a story**

- Set `title` to a **string literal** matching the value in `packages/ui-react/src/storybook/titles.ts` (`STORY.*`). Storybook 10 rejects dynamic title references.
- When renaming, update `STORY` and add the old → new mapping to `LEGACY_STORY_TITLE_MIGRATIONS` in the same file for bookmark redirects.

## React Compiler

This repo uses the **React Compiler**. Do **not** add manual memoization in app code: avoid `useMemo`, `useCallback`, and `memo` / `React.memo` unless the user explicitly asks or there is a documented exception. Write straightforward components and hooks; let the compiler optimize. Details: root `AI_RULES.md`.

See canonical patterns in existing sections under `apps/*/app/components/` or `apps/*/src/components/`.
